# VERDICT 2026-09-04: MEASURED, NOT PROMOTED (v1 chosen by the owner) - structured 68.8, prose 40.1 harness /
# 39.4 by hand, c4 203 (181/224), @1400 60.0, code 50.2, prefill flat, long-context decode 39.9 / 34.9:
# v1-level concurrency but batch-uniform, and the waves stay bimodal (so bimodality is a k>=5 property)
# (bench-results/2026-09-04-adaptive-k.md).
# Adaptive k, v5 (2026-09-04 10:51, owner: "pianifichiamolo come prossimo test"): batch-uniform mode
# with the optimistic seed (1.0) and the 0.50/0.60 band = v3 thresholds in uniform mode; completes the
# seed x mode matrix (v1/v3 per-request seed 1.0; v2 per-request seed 0.0; v4 uniform seed 0.0).
# Single stream should match v3. Four streams: every request is at 5 from the first step and the
# batch never mixes k, so if the waves settle at ~225 the bimodality was mixed-k dispatch; if the
# first wave stays slow it is a warm-up effect of the four-stream shape. Rollback: restart without TP4_ENV.
SPEC_TOKENS=5
SPEC_EXTRA_JSON='"num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size":[[1,1,5],[2,6,3]]'
EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS="--kv-cache-memory=17179869184 --moe-backend triton --scheduler-cls adaptive_k_scheduler.AdaptiveKScheduler"
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV='-v $HOME/tp4/moe-configs/E=288,N=512,device_name=NVIDIA_GB10,dtype=fp8_w8a8,block_shape=[128,128].json:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/configs/E=288,N=512,device_name=NVIDIA_GB10,dtype=fp8_w8a8,block_shape=[128,128].json:ro -v $HOME/patches/adaptive_k_scheduler.py:/opt/tp4/adaptive_k_scheduler.py:ro -e PYTHONPATH=/opt/tp4 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_MODE=batch-uniform -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_SEED=1.0 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_DOWN=0.50 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_UP=0.60'
